# Stray go-build output — `go build ./cmd/core-agent` without -o drops a
# binary at the repo root and under go/. The built binaries live in bin/
# (`task build` → bin/core-agent, `task build:lthn` → bin/lthn-agent), and
# bin/ is ignored above.
/core-agent
/go/core-agent

# superpowers design/plan scratch — not committed (shipped work lives in code)
docs/superpowers/

# PHP — installed dependencies are regenerated from composer.json/lock.
# Both paths: php/vendor/ was correct while composer.json lived in php/, and
# /vendor/ is where it installs now that composer.json is at the repo root.
php/vendor/
/vendor/

# external/ is deliberately NOT ignored, and must not exist.
#
# It used to hold submodule checkouts of the sibling dappco.re modules. Having
# the ecosystem sitting in the workspace meant agents edited it — the files
# looked local and editable, the build resolved dappco.re/* from the module
# proxy regardless, and the "fix" never shipped. Dependencies come from
# go.mod and nowhere else.
#
# No ignore rule here on purpose: if external/ ever reappears it should show
# up loudly in `git status` rather than be silently tolerated.
